# Docker build context excludes for the zetta source tree.
#
# The image Dockerfile (./Dockerfile; the e2e image's Dockerfile still lives outside this repo)
# uses this repository root as the build context and does `COPY . /src`. Without this file a host build
# directory is copied in, and its CMakeCache.txt records absolute *host* paths, so the in-image
# `cmake -S . -B build` aborts with "The current CMakeCache.txt directory ... is different than
# the directory ... where CMakeCache.txt was created" (#839).
#
# Patterns are relative to the context root, so a bare name matches only at the top level.
# That matters here: the vendored Boost-style submodules (capy, corosio, http, beast2) each
# track a real `build/` directory of Jamfiles, and those are source — never exclude `**/build`.

# ---- host build output (the #839 failure) ----
/build/
/build-*/
/cmake-build-*/
/_deps/

# Stray CMake state at any depth is never source, and is what actually poisons the in-image
# configure step.
**/CMakeCache.txt
**/CMakeFiles/
**/cmake_install.cmake
**/CTestTestfile.cmake
**/compile_commands.json
**/install_manifest.txt

# ---- version control ----
# The build needs no git: submodules are already checked out on disk and CMake never shells to git.
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.github

# ---- compiled artifacts anywhere in the tree ----
**/*.o
**/*.obj
**/*.a
**/*.so
**/*.dylib
**/*.dll
**/*.exe

# ---- node runtime data (a local run leaves a data_dir behind) ----
/zetta-data/
**/*.log

# ---- editor / tooling / OS noise ----
.cache/
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/
**/*.iml
**/*~
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/.DS_Store

# ---- local secrets / per-user config ----
**/.env
**/.env.local

# ---- not needed to compile the binary ----
# Kept deliberately short: docs and schemas are small, and schemas/ is drift-checked by the
# test build, so only the genuinely large non-build inputs are listed here.

# Local checkpoints, training corpora and generated demo data (gitignored; tens of GB on a
# training host). The binary needs none of them.
/data/checkpoints/
/data/corpora/
/data/sft-logs/
/data/demo/
